# secrets/ MUST stay first, and must stay unconditional. `secrets/*.env` is
# gitignored, so nothing about the repository being clean says it is absent
# from the build context — the file is on the developer's disk and `docker
# build .` would bake it into a layer, where `docker history` reads it back.
secrets/

.git/
.github/
.claude/
.turbo/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated inside the image by `prisma generate`. Copying a host build in
# would ship whichever platform's query engine the developer's Mac produced.
packages/db/generated/

# Nothing here excludes a workspace project's directory outright, even the six
# the API never imports: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` compares the lockfile
# against every importer `pnpm-workspace.yaml` declares, and a project whose
# package.json is missing from the context reads as a lockfile that is out of
# date. Which SOURCE is copied is decided by the COPY lines in the Dockerfile
# instead — apps/web's is never copied at all.

docs/
reference/
**/test/
**/*.test.ts
.DS_Store
